0search6\n\n**2. Once it settles, move $11 from Albert Savings → Albert Cash.** Albert says transfers **between Albert products are available immediately in most cases**. So you shouldn't have another 2–3-day ACH wait just to get it from Savings into Cash. citeturn0search6\n\n**3. From Albert Cash → SoFi, Albert has a “Direct Transfer” specifically for this.** With an eligible linked debit card, Albert says a direct transfer **typically completes within minutes**. The current fee is **$4.99**, minimum transfer is **$10**, and the daily limit is up to $500. citeturn0search4turn0search10\n\nSo for the hotel tomorrow, your plan is technically supported:\n\n**$11 settles → Savings → Albert Cash (normally immediate) → Direct Transfer to linked SoFi debit card (typically minutes).**\n\n### One catch\n\nIf you instant-transfer **only the $11**, the **$4.99 Albert fee** means this is a pretty expensive way to rescue eleven bucks. Albert's documentation says the direct-transfer fee is $4.99. citeturn0search4\n\nAlso, the screen showing **$17 Savings** does *not* mean the entire $17 is withdrawable yet. Albert specifically distinguishes total balance from settled/available funds. citeturn0search0\n\nSo yes: **if that $11 completes tomorrow, there is a documented path to get it onto SoFi within minutes rather than waiting another ACH cycle.** That's the piece I should have verified before answering you earlier."]}, "create_time": 1790295586.343124, "end_turn": true, "id": "89b350fe-5de2-4704-8144-0445550df129", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([Albert Help](https://help.albert.com/hc/en-us/articles/360048829873-How-do-I-withdraw-money-from-Savings?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 353, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "Albert Help", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {